  "summary": "Malicious code in bigops-products-savings-accounts (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package downloads a platform-specific second-stage binary over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers hosts oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev (paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe), with a DNS-over-TXT fallback via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. It writes the downloaded payload to /var/tmp/.cache_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt; (or dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt;.exe in the temp dir on Windows), makes it executable, and launches it as a detached background process (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c \"\u0026lt;file\u0026gt; \u0026amp;\" on Unix).",
